{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws","id":1383347,"title":"So is there a way to buy off flaws?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-23T06:01:07-07:00","id":1383347,"title":"So is there a way to buy off flaws?","content":"I mean, many of them seem designed with beginning characters in mind and seem like they should go away after a certain point. Are you really going to still be a Vegan after your humanity is 4 and your blood potency is 5? Yet there doesn't seem to be a mechanic for buying them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T07:55:22-07:00","id":1383367,"title":"","content":"So if Vegan is a way of saying you drink animal blood instead of humans and Humanity 4 blood potency 5 makes it so animal blood no longer gives sustenance then you don't need to buy it off you roleplayed out of it. Does going to sleep for a bit burn off blood potency like in Requiem? If your ability to live on animal blood came back I would say you would have that tendency again but would be more of an omnivore. I don't know what Humanity 4 equates too, I thought V5 didn't use it but had banes and stains tenets and touchstones?<br /> <br /> I think personality flaws can be overcome with play but physical flaws for example you'd be stuck with, other types I'd just go case by case and if you think it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T08:03:12-07:00","id":1383369,"title":"","content":"I should add I don't like the idea of buying away flaws with experience points. If you start off with a social flaw that gives you a bad reputation or clan enmity I wouldn't let a player spend 10 exp to scratch it off his or her sheet. If you did a great service for the offended clan to get back to neutral or were very helpful over time to the powers that be in the city you can change your rep but I'd make you role play it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T10:11:19-07:00","id":1383387,"title":"","content":"In V5, no. The Flaw is there to provide an RP opportunity for you and the ST; your example of BPing out of the Vegan flaw is a very, very corner case in the expectations of the game. Most of the character expectation is to play characters who are younger, who aren't going to have hundreds of years of experience under their belt to have massive amounts of BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T10:22:12-07:00","id":1383395,"title":"","content":"As elmerg says, there are no specific rules for this. But the sidebar on page 180 talks about removing Flaws through gameplay\u2014maybe you're Destitute, but you get a boon from a Ventrue, and ask for a minor source of income (Resources 1).<br /> <br /> The sidebar mostly focuses on gaining and losing Backgrounds, but does mention Flaws as well, so I'd apply the same rules: if you remove chargen Flaws during play, you assign those Flaw points to something else. Maybe you can no longer feed on animals, but you still have ethical concerns about feeding on humans, so you get rid of Vegan and replace it with Feeding Restriction (Must Consent) and something else to add up to the same number of dots. Maybe you establish a Haven in play, so the No Haven flaw no longer applies, but that new Haven ends up being Haunted. Etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T15:20:27-07:00","id":1383454,"title":"","content":"Most games I play say that removing of Flaws depends on ST approval (based on your PC's roleplay and events in the game) and costs a number of XP equivalent to the flaw x2 (or maybe more). Obviously certain Flaws can be more easily removed than others, and some Flaws are likely to be permanent. Sometimes there needs to be a special story involved, and other times it just requires passage of time or certain experiences in the routine course of game.<br /> <br /> I don't think people should take Flaws with the idea that they'll be removed later. As an ST I would not be look well on that. But there are plenty of occasions when the Flaw no longer makes sense, and the PC should work with the Player on how to remove it, and then pay for that with XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-26-2020, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T15:56:53-07:00","id":1383459,"title":"","content":"In short appropriate Roleplay.<br /> <br /> With the Vegan example, after the 200 years passed to reach a BP of 3 the character has either come to terms with what he is and must do to survive,(loses the flaw) choses voluntary final death over accepting what he is,(maybe does so long before reaching an age of 200 years) spirals down on his humanity in an endless alternation of hunger frenzy and clarity while clinging to his \u201cnot feeding from humans\u201d until he loses to the beast and/or is put down, or falls to torpor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:53:34-07:00","id":1383482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws#post1383347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, many of them seem designed with beginning characters in mind and seem like they should go away after a certain point. Are you really going to still be a Vegan after your humanity is 4 and your blood potency is 5? Yet there doesn't seem to be a mechanic for buying them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are not published rules for it.<br /> <br /> We need some. Badly.<br /> <br /> Fingers crossed for the Players Guide.<br /> <br /> Or, I suppose, it could be that vampires don't lose their initial flaws over time. If you have an enemy, you will<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RespawningEnemies\" target=\"_blank\"> find a new enemy</a> every time the old one is killed off. If you are vegan early on, you just starve after you reach BP3. If you have stalkers, you will always, always have obsessed fans.<br /> <br /> Homebrew-wise, I would allow flaws to be bought off by spending xp (at a cost of 1 xp per dot of flaw) assuming there is <i>some</i> sort of in-story resolution to the flaw. (Killing the enemy, almost dying from not feeding on humans, ending your career as a teen pop idol to get rid of stalkers, etc.)<br /> <br /> If somebody really doesn't want to play their flaw, and they're willing to have a short arc resolving it, what does it serve to make them play it? Lots of works of fiction have characters that begin with minor flaws that seem to get resolved early on. How many fictional characters have &quot;<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CallToAdventure\" target=\"_blank\">shy and overly cautious</a>&quot;, but get over it as soon as the action begins?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25507_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25507\" data-vbnamecard=\"25507\">nobby</a> <br /> <br /> It need not take anywhere near 200 years.<br /> <br /> Blood Potency 3 is the minimum BP for seventh generation vampires. If a sixth gen embraces somebody, they are BP3 on the first night. Admittedly, this is not a common starting power level for a game.<br /> <br /> The cost for new levels of Blood Potency is (new rating x10). So, a book standard fledgling starts with BP 1 will need 50 xp to get there. This a pile of xp, but not impossible.<br /> <br /> Other book-standard power levels do exist. For example, a book standard ancilla starts with 35xp. Reaching BP3 shouldn't be <i>too</i> hard, given they start at BP 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T05:54:13-07:00","id":1383757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws?p=1383482#post1383482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If somebody really doesn't want to play their flaw, and they're willing to have a short arc resolving it, what does it serve to make them play it? Lots of works of fiction have characters that begin with minor flaws that seem to get resolved early on. How many fictional characters have &quot;<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CallToAdventure\" target=\"_blank\">shy and overly cautious</a>&quot;, but get over it as soon as the action begins?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sure, but if the player doesn't want to play the flaw, why pick it in the first place? Picking a flaw basically comes down to saying hey ST this is something I want explore, play with, have in in the story. Design wise the necessity to pick flaws under V5 character creation is there because flaws create drama, crate conflict, lead to character driven story and also force players to make multidimensional characters that are tied to the world around them.<br /> If you don't want that you can always change things so that your players start without flaws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws?p=1383482#post1383482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It need not take anywhere near 200 years.<br /> <br /> Blood Potency 3 is the minimum BP for seventh generation vampires. If a sixth gen embraces somebody, they are BP3 on the first night. Admittedly, this is not a common starting power level for a game.<br /> <br /> The cost for new levels of Blood Potency is (new rating x10). So, a book standard fledgling starts with BP 1 will need 50 xp to get there. This a pile of xp, but not impossible.<br /> <br /> Other book-standard power levels do exist. For example, a book standard ancilla starts with 35xp. Reaching BP3 shouldn't be <i>too</i> hard, given they start at BP 2.</div> </div> </div> </div> The book also says that naturally BP increases at a rate of about 1 BP per 100 years, this speed can be increased through narrative justification, \u201cespecially intense experiences\u201d which I doubt a Vegan would have, without seriously confronting his flaw, since he is someone who shies away from his vampiric nature.<br /> <br /> And yes you can, in theory make a character with BP 3 and the Vegan flaw. But that is on you. It is a legitimate concept for a Vampire to not be able to cope with their unlife and not make it. Weather you and your ST want to play that is a different question.<br /> <br /> As for rules, they do exist, they are not crunchy but they are there. But V5 wants you to focus on narrative aspects anyway.<br /> <br /> &quot;GAINING AND LOSING<br /> ADVANTAGES<br /> Events during the chronicle can<br /> change a character\u2019s Advantages<br /> and Flaws, especially Backgrounds.<br /> A Haven can burn down, an Ally<br /> can turn on you if you betray<br /> them, or the cops can gun down<br /> a Retainer for no reason at all.<br /> Conversely, by desperate quest<br /> or clever machination you can<br /> acquire an Advantage; the dots<br /> fluctuate along with your character\u2019s<br /> fortunes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","user":"nobby","date":". 04-25-2020, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T08:12:38-07:00","id":1383772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws?p=1383757#post1383757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> Yeah sure, but if the player doesn't want to play the flaw, why pic it in the first place?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do want to play the flaw. Right now I wouldn't even consider it a &quot;flaw&quot; so much as a personality trait of my fledgeling character. However, since the ST said there would be timeskips eventually, Big ones. I'd rather not still have this personality quirk as an elder. My core idea was that I would start as a Humanity 8 Farmer-Pred who was treated like crap by his sire, I'd lose two or three Hums during play, and that during the timeskip I would have spent decades with the Sabbat. I wanted to RP my char slowly moving from a good church boy to a savage.<br /> <br /> When I made the char, I kind of vaguely assumed you could buy off flaws without checking it. Figured I'd buy off Vegan with the timeskip XP. It's only just before I made this thread that I double-checked the book and realized, &quot;wait, there's no mechanic for buying off flaws in this edition.&quot; Soooo....after the timeskip I'll be an elder Sabbat who is still a Farmer pred with the Vegan flaw???<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T08:31:40-07:00","id":1383774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws?p=1383772#post1383772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do want to play the flaw. Right now I wouldn't even consider it a &quot;flaw&quot; so much as a personality trait of my fledgeling character. However, since the ST said there would be timeskips eventually, Big ones. I'd rather not still have this personality quirk as an elder. My core idea was that I would start as a Humanity 8 Farmer-Pred who was treated like crap by his sire, I'd lose two or three Hums during play, and that during the timeskip I would have spent decades with the Sabbat. I wanted to RP my char slowly moving from a good church boy to a savage.<br /> <br /> When I made the char, I kind of vaguely assumed you could buy off flaws without checking it. Figured I'd buy off Vegan with the timeskip XP. It's only just before I made this thread that I double-checked the book and realized, &quot;wait, there's no mechanic for buying off flaws in this edition.&quot; Soooo....after the timeskip I'll be an elder Sabbat who is still a Farmer pred with the Vegan flaw???<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book talks about things like this changing based on the narrative as well; so in this instance, you and the ST should swap out for a flaw with the same dot requirement. This is talked about on the sidebar on pg. 180. So instead of losing the flaw, you'd just swap it for something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T15:20:24-07:00","id":1383852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws?p=1383757#post1383757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah sure, but if the player doesn't want to play the flaw, why pick it in the first place? Picking a flaw basically comes down to saying hey ST this is something I want explore, play with, have in in the story. Design wise the necessity to pick flaws under V5 character creation is there because flaws create drama, crate conflict, lead to character driven story and also force players to make multidimensional characters that are tied to the world around them.<br /> If you don't want that you can always change things so that your players start without flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good point that players should be careful of the flaws they choose, or risk being stuck with flaws that are more restrictive than they realized. I have a lot of sympathy for that sort of strict interpretation of the rules. Yes, it is collaborative storytelling, but at some point it is also a game system, with dice and win/loss/mostly draw conditions. If players don't want to put in the time to learn the rules, well, playing a sub-par character with all the settings set to &quot;difficult&quot; might teach them the importance of doing so. (see also: choosing Nosferatu in VtMB)<br /> <br /> There are a few small problems with that position, which make me pause before being <i>too</i> hard-ass of an ST:<br /> <br /> 1. Some players, being inexperienced, may blithely take a (literally for the pc) fatal flaw without realizing what they are doing. Now, this is why STs should review characters before play starts, but no one can catch everything. Given V5 is still a relatively new system, and the rules presentation is... let's charitably say... &quot;not designed with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usability\" target=\"_blank\">usability</a> as the main goal&quot;. Some flexibility is called for when the player's vision of their pc's story-arc doesn't work with the mechanics, or when unforeseen synergies arise.<br /> <br /> 2. It is not necessary for a character to have additional flaws to be interesting in V5. Vampires, by definition, have a giant pile of flaws. Arguably quite a bit more than most fictional characters. Hamlet may have been indecisive, but he was able to be indecisive at brunch without bursting into flame. Scarlett O'Hara may have been oblivious to the suffering of others, but she never had to make a roll to resist frenzy. If nothing else, every V5 pc has clan or thinblood flaws already built in. The reason it still works and doesn't feel frustrating for the players is because all the pcs have the same massive flaws. Few VtM sessions start with, &quot;The next day, at brunch, you all go fwoosh!&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Requiring the flaws freely chosen at chagen to be permanent closes off story possibilities, not opens them up. Fictional characters with flaws that cannot possibly change are less compelling than those who might reform. Even if the character never reforms, the open question of their fate maintains interest. A very reasonable plan for an ST running a sandbox campaign would be to just drop pcs off in a city and challenge them to remove their flaws. You could run a whole chronicle of complications out of that. But, not if removal is not a clearly available possibility under the rules.<br /> <br /> 4. Some flaws, aside from being overly constraining, as in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a>'s situation, are just nonsensical in some stories. Let's say you have Stalkers as a flaw because you are a world-famous KPop star. You go into torpor in a hidden cave for a hundred years. How does one justify screaming fans greeting you when you awaken? It's nice the system says the flaws can be changed, but by not giving us a mechanic for doing so they have really done nothing the golden rule doesn't do.<br /> <br /> 5. As for the vague mention of being ability to alter pcs in-game, there is a major problem. It's fine we here agree that a reasonable solution could be homebrewed when we are STing. What if you're not the storyteller? Having published canon, RAW rules exist so STs can run games, but also so players have some idea what they can expect during the game without having to convince their ST. If there were a published mechanic for changing flaws, it would be reliably available to non-ST players. (Plus, STs wouldn't have to constantly homebrew stuff on the fly.)<br /> <br /> 6. The entire concept the player has for the character's story-arc may involve removing their flaw. Often such a desire is the basis for a <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Film/TheWizardOfOz\" target=\"_blank\">whole quest</a>. If there is no mechanic for removing the flaw, then what's the point of the story arc? If such a character has no clear path to success, at best the whole thing can devolve into nihilism. &quot;I am vegan, and so I know I am not immortal. I shall die the final death when I reach BP 3.&quot; At worst, it can breed wangst.<br /> <br /> 7. Around a table where the ST takes such a hardline, frustrated players may notice there are game systems where it is nearly impossible to build a character which is straight-up unable to survive in the campaign world. D&amp;D 5e may have it's flaws, and some builds are marginally more or less effective in play. It's nearly impossible for a new player to accidentally create an entirely ineffective character using the standard rules. It does not have the equivalent of Vegan just sitting there, looking all innocent, waiting for inexperienced players to choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T18:24:07-07:00","id":1383887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws?p=1383852#post1383852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Some players, being inexperienced, may blithely take a (literally for the pc) fatal flaw without realizing what they are doing. Now, this is why STs should review characters before play starts, but no one can catch everything. Given V5 is still a relatively new system, and the rules presentation is... let's charitably say... &quot;not designed with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usability\" target=\"_blank\">usability</a> as the main goal&quot;. Some flexibility is called for when the player's vision of their pc's story-arc doesn't work with the mechanics, or when unforeseen synergies arise.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Oh I never meant this as some sort of hard-ass rules approach. My core assumption here is that the player chooses consciously what they want to play. And flaws are cards you hand the ST that say \u201chere are the problems I want in my characters story to be dealt with\u201d. So what I meant is for example building a PC with BP 3 and the vegan flaw means saying \u201c I want to play a character who has to drink human blood but can't bring himself to drink from a human. So he will be constantly low on WP and hungry and frenzy a lot and probably burn through his humanity. THIS is the character and story I want to play.\u201d<br /> <br /> Of course, if a player creates a character that doesn't work, that's different. But when a player realizes the character doesn't work how they imagined or isn't as fun/interesting to play as they imagined you don't need rules to by of flaws, you sit down with that player and rework that character or crate a new character.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the rest, I state again appropriate roleplay changes/deals with flaws.<br /> As for rules to that effect, to quote the core-book again:<br /> <br /> &quot;GAINING AND LOSING<br /> ADVANTAGES<br /> Events during the chronicle can<br /> change a character\u2019s Advantages<br /> and Flaws... the dots<br /> fluctuate along with your character\u2019s<br /> fortunes. \u201d<br /> <br /> So in answer to your your 4th point, the mechanic is quiet clear. Your stalker dies of old age while you are in torpor? You no longer have a stalker. Congrats flaw resolved. No further mechanics needed. What more, in terms of mechanics would you need there? Wouldn't it be way more nonsensical to say you need to buy of flaws with x amount of xp, so after a hundred years in torpor you need to spend xp or somehow the still mortal stalker also is still alive waiting to stalk you again. Isn't \u201cwhat makes sense in the narrative \u201d the way more simple and elegant solution?<br /> <br /> I think I really don't understand what kind of mechanic you would want that would help there. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T04:25:33-07:00","id":1383938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383347-so-is-there-a-way-to-buy-off-flaws#post1383347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, many of them seem designed with beginning characters in mind and seem like they should go away after a certain point. Are you really going to still be a Vegan after your humanity is 4 and your blood potency is 5? Yet there doesn't seem to be a mechanic for buying them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanic is called &quot;playing the game&quot;. Depending on your ST, do the right things and you may be able to lessen or even erase the effects of your flaws possibly gaining new and different ones in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}